From 94dec5c0417264ab2710ac2af99a965e776c0808 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 31 Mar 2026 12:46:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] media: meson: vdec: fix esparser stall when capture
 buffer not in queue

When the firmware signals a decoded frame but the corresponding capture
buffer has already been delivered to userspace and not yet re-queued,
amvdec_dst_buf_done_idx() logs an error and returns without decrementing
esparser_queued_bufs or rescheduling the esparser work queue.

This causes two problems:
 - The esparser_queued_bufs counter drifts upward, eventually breaking
   EOS detection which checks for the counter reaching <= 1
 - The esparser work queue is not kicked, potentially stalling input
   processing

Fix by decrementing the counter and rescheduling the esparser work
even when the buffer is not found. Downgrade the message from dev_err
to dev_dbg since this is a known transient condition during normal
operation with MPEG1/2 and other codecs that can temporarily outpace
userspace buffer recycling.

Additionally, handle the MREG_WAIT_BUFFER register in the MPEG1/2
ISR. The firmware writes to this register when it needs a free output
buffer, but the driver never acknowledged it, which could cause the
firmware to stall or re-use un-recycled buffers.

Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c |  4 ++++
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
index 14ff90c7c7eed..9c1079d60e094 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
@@ -174,6 +174,10 @@ static irqreturn_t codec_mpeg12_threaded_isr(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
+	/* Acknowledge any buffer-wait request from firmware */
+	if (amvdec_read_dos(core, MREG_WAIT_BUFFER))
+		amvdec_write_dos(core, MREG_WAIT_BUFFER, 0);
+
 	reg = amvdec_read_dos(core, MREG_BUFFEROUT);
 	if (!reg)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
index 019a91f9b2bea..deaf7358345ed 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
@@ -429,9 +429,18 @@ void amvdec_dst_buf_done_idx(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 					      sess->fw_idx_to_vb2_idx[buf_idx]);
 
 	if (!vbuf) {
-		dev_err(dev,
+		dev_dbg(dev,
 			"Buffer %u done but it doesn't exist in m2m_ctx\n",
 			buf_idx);
+		/*
+		 * The firmware completed a buffer that isn't in the m2m
+		 * ready queue — it was already delivered to userspace and
+		 * not yet re-queued. We must still decrement the esparser
+		 * counter and kick the esparser work queue, otherwise the
+		 * counter drifts and EOS detection breaks.
+		 */
+		atomic_dec(&sess->esparser_queued_bufs);
+		schedule_work(&sess->esparser_queue_work);
 		return;
 	}
 
